@lang en
-- Tests of ie-interpretation-time.l4: days of rest, recess or holiday (an input), working days, week-days, and the Schedule's time words.
-- The holidays used here are INPUTS written for these tests; they are not claims about any calendar, and the module contains no holiday calendar.
-- Calendar premises: 2026-01-01 is a Thursday, 2026-01-03 a Saturday, 2026-01-04 a Sunday, 2026-01-05 a Monday (asserted in tests-periods.l4).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ie-interpretation-time`

§ `Inputs supplied by the tests`

-- A "day of rest, recess or holiday" for the tests: every Saturday and Sunday, and two dates the test calls holidays (Thursday 2026-01-01 and Monday 2026-01-05).
`holidays supplied by the tests` MEANS
    GIVEN d YIELD elem d (LIST (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 1 5))

`days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` MEANS
    GIVEN d YIELD (NOT `is weekday` d) OR `holidays supplied by the tests` d

`no public holidays` MEANS
    GIVEN d YIELD FALSE

`every day a public holiday` MEANS
    GIVEN d YIELD TRUE

§ `The Act has no rule moving a last day: it is returned when it is an ordinary day, and the module refuses when it is a day of rest or holiday`

-- Friday 2026-01-02: an ordinary day, returned as it stands
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (YMD 2026 1 2) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2
-- Monday 2026-01-12 and Tuesday 2026-01-06: ordinary days (a Monday after a weekend is not itself a rest day)
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (YMD 2026 1 12) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 12
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (YMD 2026 1 6) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 6
-- Saturday and Sunday: two in a row; the last day is a rest day either way
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (YMD 2026 1 3) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a last day that falls on a day of rest, recess or holiday; another enactment or rules of court may have one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (YMD 2026 1 4) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests`
-- a holiday on a weekday (Thursday 2026-01-01; Monday 2026-01-05)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (YMD 2026 1 1) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (YMD 2026 1 5) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests`
-- the same date with no rest days supplied is an ordinary day
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (YMD 2026 1 3) `no public holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 3
-- a period whose last day lands on a Sunday: one calendar month from 1 August 2025 ends on Sunday 31 August 2025
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (`the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 8 1)) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests`
-- a period whose last day lands on an ordinary day: one calendar month from 1 September 2025 ends on Tuesday 30 September 2025
#ASSERT `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (`the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 9 1)) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` EQUALS YMD 2025 9 30
-- a period whose last day cannot be placed does not become placeable by the rest-day step
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period, allowing for days of rest, recess or holiday` (`the last day of a period of` 1 `calendar months beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2025 1 31)) `days of rest or holiday supplied by the tests` BECAUSE "the Act has no rule for a period of calendar months that does not begin on the first day of a month"

§ `Schedule Pt 2 "working day": a day which is not a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday`

#ASSERT `is a working day` (YMD 2026 1 6) `holidays supplied by the tests`
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (YMD 2026 1 3) `holidays supplied by the tests`
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (YMD 2026 1 4) `holidays supplied by the tests`
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (YMD 2026 1 5) `holidays supplied by the tests`
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (YMD 2026 1 1) `holidays supplied by the tests`
#ASSERT `is a working day` (YMD 2026 1 5) `no public holidays`

§ `N working days from a day: the first day is included if it is a working day (s 18(h)), and only working days count`

-- 1 working day from Thursday 2026-01-01 (a holiday) is Friday 2026-01-02
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, public holidays being` `holidays supplied by the tests` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 2
-- 2 working days: Friday 2, then Sat, Sun, Monday 5 (a holiday) are skipped, Tuesday 6
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 2 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 1) `, public holidays being` `holidays supplied by the tests` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 6
-- begun on a Saturday: Sat, Sun, and the holiday Monday do not count, so the first working day is Tuesday 6
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 3) `, public holidays being` `holidays supplied by the tests` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 6
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 3 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 6) `, public holidays being` `holidays supplied by the tests` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 8
-- 5 working days from Tuesday 6: 6, 7, 8, 9, then Monday 12
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 5 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 6) `, public holidays being` `holidays supplied by the tests` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 12
-- with no public holidays: 5 working days from Monday 5 is Friday 9; 6 is Monday 12
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 5 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 5) `, public holidays being` `no public holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 9
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 6 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 5) `, public holidays being` `no public holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 12
-- a first day that is a working day is itself day 1
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 6) `, public holidays being` `no public holidays` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 6
-- not a period; and a calendar in which no day is a working day is not searched for ever
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 0 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 6) `, public holidays being` `no public holidays` BECAUSE "a period must be a whole number of units, at least one"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 1 `working days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 6) `, public holidays being` `every day a public holiday` BECAUSE "no day was found within the search limit"

§ `Schedule Pt 1 "week-day": a day which is not a Sunday`

#ASSERT `is a week-day` (YMD 2026 1 5)
#ASSERT `is a week-day` (YMD 2026 1 3)
#ASSERT NOT `is a week-day` (YMD 2026 1 4)
-- 6 week-days from Monday 2026-01-05: Monday to Saturday
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 6 `week-days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 10
-- 7 week-days: the Sunday 11 is skipped
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 7 `week-days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 12
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `week-days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 4) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 5
#ASSERT `the last day of a period of` 1 `week-days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 5) EQUALS YMD 2026 1 5
#ASSERT REFUSED `the last day of a period of` 0 `week-days beginning on or reckoned from` (YMD 2026 1 5) BECAUSE "a period must be a whole number of units, at least one"

§ `Schedule Pt 1 "week": between midnight on a Saturday and midnight on the following Saturday; "midnight" is the point at which a day ends, so a week runs Sunday to Saturday`

#ASSERT (`the week containing` (YMD 2026 1 1))'s `its first day` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 28
#ASSERT (`the week containing` (YMD 2026 1 1))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 3
#ASSERT (`the week containing` (YMD 2026 1 4))'s `its first day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 4
#ASSERT (`the week containing` (YMD 2026 1 4))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 10
#ASSERT (`the week containing` (YMD 2026 1 10))'s `its first day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 4
#ASSERT (`the week containing` (YMD 2026 1 10))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2026 1 10
#ASSERT `is the first day of a week` (YMD 2026 1 4)
#ASSERT NOT `is the first day of a week` (YMD 2026 1 3)
#ASSERT NOT `is the first day of a week` (YMD 2026 1 5)

§ `Schedule Pt 1 "month" (a calendar month) and "year" (12 months beginning 1 January); "financial year" and "local financial year" (coextensive with a calendar year)`

#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2024 2 10))'s `its first day` EQUALS YMD 2024 2 1
#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2024 2 10))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2024 2 29
#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2025 2 10))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2025 2 28
#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2025 12 31))'s `its first day` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 1
#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2025 12 31))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT (`the calendar month containing` (YMD 2025 4 15))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2025 4 30
#ASSERT (`the year containing` (YMD 2025 7 16))'s `its first day` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT (`the year containing` (YMD 2025 7 16))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT (`the exchequer financial year containing` (YMD 2025 7 16))'s `its first day` EQUALS YMD 2025 1 1
#ASSERT (`the exchequer financial year containing` (YMD 2025 7 16))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2025 12 31
#ASSERT (`the local financial year containing` (YMD 2024 2 29))'s `its first day` EQUALS YMD 2024 1 1
#ASSERT (`the local financial year containing` (YMD 2024 2 29))'s `its last day` EQUALS YMD 2024 12 31

§ `Section 18(i): a time expressed by reference to an hour is determined by another Act, which is not in this text`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the clock time of a specified hour in an enactment` 9 BECAUSE "the Standard Time (Amendment) Act 1971 is not in the text of this Act and is not encoded"
